Once upon a time, in the lush jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, a Gnome Warlock named Gimli was on a quest to level up his Succubus pet. Gimli was an adventurous soul, always seeking new challenges and experiences. He had heard tales of the powerful creatures that roamed the jungles, and he was eager to test his skills against them.

Gimli's Succubus, named Faye, was a formidable companion. She had a unique ability that allowed her to summon a temporary minion, which proved to be incredibly useful in combat. However, despite her impressive skills, Gimli often found himself longing for the power of a Voidwalker.

One day, while exploring a dense part of the jungle, Gimli and Faye stumbled upon a group of powerful creatures. Gimli knew that he would need all the help he could get, so he summoned Faye's temporary minion. The battle was fierce, but with the combined strength of Faye and her minion, Gimli was able to defeat the creatures and emerge victorious.

As Gimli and Faye continued their journey, Gimli began to understand the true value of Faye's unique ability. While a Voidwalker may have been more powerful in certain situations, the flexibility and adaptability provided by Faye's temporary minion proved to be invaluable in the ever-changing environment of Stranglethorn Vale.

And so, Gimli and Faye continued their adventures, the Gnome Warlock and his Succubus pet, conquering the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale and proving that the power of teamwork and adaptability could overcome even the most formidable of foes.

The answer to the riddle is that most Warlocks prefer Voidwalkers because of their permanent presence, while the Succubus' temporary minion ability provides flexibility and adaptability, making them a better choice for leveling and questing in certain situations.
